  #line-at(166.44pt, 299.16pt, "Abstract: ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 9pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(204.96pt, 299.16pt, "Potable water utilities are currently making great efforts to reduce leakage rates and assure ")
  #line-at(166.44pt, 312.12pt, "long-term supply to the population due to the challenges of climate change, growing population ")
  #line-at(166.44pt, 325.08pt, "and water shortage scenarios that have been on them over the last years. One of the most employed ")
  #line-at(166.44pt, 338.16pt, "methods to reduce leakage includes the installation of pressurereducing valves along the water dis-")
  #line-at(166.44pt, 351.12pt, "tribution network and the utilization of pressure management schemes. Pressure management in-")
  #line-at(166.44pt, 364.08pt, "cludes different types of control models, which are applied according to the requirements of each ")
  #line-at(166.44pt, 377.16pt, "site. The most advanced and sophisticated scheme is critical point control, which relies on a flow ")
  #line-at(166.44pt, 390.12pt, "signal from a measuring device or online communication between the critical point and the valve. ")
  #line-at(166.44pt, 403.08pt, "This paper proposes the utilization of a seasonal autoregressive integrated moving average, or the ")
  #line-at(166.44pt, 416.16pt, "SARIMA model, to correlate pressure at the outlet of the valve and pressure on the critical point of ")
  #line-at(166.44pt, 429.12pt, "the area supplied, aiming to set a fixed pressure in the critical point. The SARIMA model is devel-")
  #line-at(166.44pt, 442.08pt, "oped according to historical data logged in the field and then validated. Later, the SARIMA model ")
  #line-at(166.44pt, 455.16pt, "was tested on a real location in the village of Noja, Spain. The analysis of the field test results prove ")
  #line-at(167.04pt, 468.12pt, "that the proposed model is feasible to be used since there is no significance difference between the ")
  #line-at(167.04pt, 481.08pt, "target values set in the critical point and the real values measured in the field. The research proves ")
  #line-at(167.04pt, 494.16pt, "that the SARIMA model can be used as an alternative for critical point control in water distribution ")
  #line-at(167.04pt, 507.12pt, "networks when no flow signal is available or when communication between the critical point and ")
  #line-at(167.04pt, 520.08pt, "the pressure reducing valve is not an option. ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 9pt, weight: "bold", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(167.04pt, 545.16pt, "Keywords: ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 9pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(213.6pt, 545.16pt, "pressure management; pressure reducing valve; critical point control; SARIMA model ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 9.96pt, weight: "bold", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(167.04pt, 596.76pt, "1. Introduction ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 9.96pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(188.4pt, 612.6pt, "The utilization of pressure reducing valves (PRV) in water distribution networks ")
  #line-at(167.04pt, 625.32pt, "(WDN) is widely extended as a tool to reduce leakage [1–3], lower burst frequency [4], ")
  #line-at(167.04pt, 638.16pt, "improve level of service to the customers [5] and, to a minor extent, and mainly under ")
  #line-at(167.04pt, 651pt, "water scarcity situations, manage customer consumption [6,7]. Most of the water utilities ")
  #line-at(167.04pt, 663.84pt, "across the world have implemented working plans to install this type of valves to achieve ")
  #line-at(167.04pt, 676.68pt, "one or various of the mentioned targets [8]. Moreover, scientific production over the last ")
  #line-at(167.04pt, 689.4pt, "years related to the employment of PRV in WDN has grown drastically [9]. Over the last ")
  #line-at(167.04pt, 702.24pt, "years, it has also become popular the utilization of pumps as turbine (PATs) in WDN, ")
  #line-at(167.04pt, 715.08pt, "which, in addition to the pressure reducing function, can also generate energy [10,11]. ")
  #line-at(167.04pt, 727.92pt, "Different methods have been developed in the literature for the optimal location of PATs ")
  #line-at(167.04pt, 740.76pt, "[12,13]. Despite more research and experience still required, PATs are identified as a clear ")
  #line-at(167.04pt, 753.48pt, "future alternative to PRVs from both an economic and a sustainability point of view [14]. ")
  #line-at(188.4pt, 766.32pt, "A PRV whichs a hydraulic control valvewhichch reduces upstream pressure to a sta-")
  #line-at(166.44pt, 779.16pt, "ble downstream pressure regardless of flow or upstream pressure fluctuations. The ")
