  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 9.96pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(166.44pt, 102.24pt, "at the installation site and it does not require the critical point of the system to be con-")
  #line-at(166.44pt, 115.08pt, "nected with the PRV. As a result, the installation and commissioning process for the utili-")
  #line-at(166.44pt, 127.92pt, "ties is easier and also lowers the investment required. ")
  #line-at(187.68pt, 140.64pt, "The use of statistical and mathematical techniques for the analysis of time series has ")
  #line-at(166.44pt, 153.48pt, "been known since the 19th century. A time series is a set of observations ordered or plo")
  #line-at(542.16pt, 153.48pt, "Ĵ")
  #line-at(548.4pt, 153.48pt, "ed ")
  #line-at(166.44pt, 166.32pt, "against time and conclusions drawn from them. In the early 1970s, Box and Jenkins (1976) ")
  #line-at(166.44pt, 179.16pt, "[32] devised a statistical methodology for time series analysis, applied to different scien-")
  #line-at(166.44pt, 192pt, "tific branches, which were la")
  #line-at(291.48pt, 192pt, "Ĵ")
  #line-at(297.72pt, 192pt, "er named as ARIMA models. The ARIMA model, in its sim-")
  #line-at(166.44pt, 204.72pt, "plest version, has only three components that give the model its name: AR for autoregres-")
  #line-at(166.44pt, 217.56pt, "sive, I for integrated and MA for moving averages. Each part is represented by a positive ")
  #line-at(166.44pt, 230.4pt, "integer (p,d,q). AR, or autoregressive, models are used under the condition that past val-")
  #line-at(166.44pt, 243.24pt, "ues condition or correlate with current values, and MA, or moving average, models take ")
  #line-at(166.44pt, 256.08pt, "into account past residuals to correctly fit the model. The application of ARIMA models ")
  #line-at(166.44pt, 268.8pt, "requires the time series to be stationary: mean and variance are stable over time. The ")
  #line-at(166.44pt, 281.64pt, "SARIMA model is an extension of the ARIMA model that allows modeling non-stationary ")
  #line-at(166.44pt, 294.48pt, "series. ")
  #line-at(187.68pt, 307.32pt, "The ARIMA model has been employed in numerous research fields. For example, it ")
  #line-at(166.44pt, 320.16pt, "has been used for modeling and forecasting water consumption by Zhou et al. [33], Jain ")
  #line-at(166.44pt, 332.88pt, "and Ormsbee [34], Wong et al. [35], Caiado [36] and Baraun et al. [37]. In the medical re-")
  #line-at(166.44pt, 345.72pt, "search field, Liu et al. [38] explored the demographic characteristics of acute hemorrhagic ")
  #line-at(166.44pt, 358.56pt, "conjunctivitis using a SARIMA model. Saz [39] modeled and forecast the inflation rate in ")
  #line-at(166.44pt, 371.4pt, "developing countries, focusing on Turkey and Otu et al. [40] on Nigeria. Makoni et al. [41] ")
  #line-at(166.44pt, 384.24pt, "forecast international tourist arrivals in Zimbabwe. Divisekara et al. [42] used the ")
  #line-at(166.44pt, 396.96pt, "SARIMA model to forecast the price of red lentils in Canada, the largest producer in the ")
  #line-at(166.44pt, 409.8pt, "world. Martinez-Acosta et al. [43] used the model for time series from monthly rainfall ")
  #line-at(166.44pt, 422.64pt, "and Koohfar et al. [44] for electric vehicle charging demand. Dabral and Murry [45] used ")
  #line-at(166.44pt, 435.48pt, "SARIMA models for monthly, weekly and daily monsoon rainfall time series. Valipur [46] ")
  #line-at(166.44pt, 448.32pt, "validated SARIMA models to forecast long-term runoff in the United States. Akipanar and ")
  #line-at(166.44pt, 461.04pt, "Yumusak [47] applied ARIMA models to forecast gas consumption in Turkey to improve ")
  #line-at(166.44pt, 473.88pt, "demand forecasting. ")
  #line-at(187.68pt, 486.72pt, "This paper describes a time-based open-loop CPC model, with SARIMA applied to ")
  #line-at(166.44pt, 499.56pt, "pressure management (PM) in WDN. The model relates the ratio of the system critical ")
  #line-at(166.44pt, 512.4pt, "point pressure (")
  #set text(font: "Arial", size: 9.96pt, weight: "regular", style: "italic", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(238.32pt, 512.4pt, "P3")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 9.96pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(249.48pt, 512.4pt, ") to the pressure at the outlet of the valve (")
  #set text(font: "Arial", size: 9.96pt, weight: "regular", style: "italic", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(447pt, 512.4pt, "P2)")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 9.96pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(461.52pt, 512.4pt, " as a function of time ")
  #line-at(166.44pt, 525.12pt, "(")
  #set text(font: "Arial", size: 9.96pt, weight: "regular", style: "italic", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(169.8pt, 525.12pt, "P3/P2")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 9.96pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(195pt, 525.12pt, "), creating a predictive model which assures target pressure in the critical point of ")
  #line-at(166.44pt, 537.96pt, "the WDN. The model has been developed and tested on a real location in the village of ")
  #line-at(166.44pt, 550.8pt, "Noja in northern Spain. This village is characterized by great seasonal demand variation ")
  #line-at(166.44pt, 563.64pt, "throughout the year. Currently, Noja water utility is applying CPC based on an open-loop ")
  #line-at(166.44pt, 576.48pt, "control model, which relates headloss between the outlet of the valve and the critical point ")
  #line-at(166.44pt, 589.32pt, "against the flow at the inlet of the WDN. This pressure-control strategy has been identified ")
  #line-at(166.44pt, 602.04pt, "as the most beneficial by the water utility since it allows to keep pressure at the minimum ")
  #line-at(166.44pt, 614.88pt, "level in the WDN, while assuring the right level of service to the customers, under the ")
  #line-at(166.44pt, 627.72pt, "challenging seasonal demand pa")
  #line-at(313.44pt, 627.72pt, "Ĵ")
  #line-at(319.68pt, 627.72pt, "ern of the area. However, due to the criticality of the ")
  #line-at(166.44pt, 640.56pt, "installation, especially during summer and bank holidays when the area is full of tourists, ")
  #line-at(166.44pt, 653.4pt, "it would be desirable to have an alternative control scheme in case of malfunction of the ")
  #line-at(166.44pt, 666.12pt, "flow meter to maintain target pressure in the critical point regardless of the flow measure-")
  #line-at(166.44pt, 678.96pt, "ment. This fact motivates this research and the elaboration of this paper. The results show ")
  #line-at(166.44pt, 691.8pt, "that the new time-controlled model might be applied with satisfactory results and can be ")
  #line-at(166.44pt, 704.64pt, "a backup alternative for water utilities in situations where they cannot apply FM or tradi-")
  #line-at(166.44pt, 717.48pt, "tional CPC based on flow measurements or by connecting the PRV with the ")
  #set text(font: "Arial", size: 9.96pt, weight: "regular", style: "italic", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(502.32pt, 717.48pt, "P3")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 9.96pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(513.48pt, 717.48pt, ". ")
]

