  #line-at(166.44pt, 118.08pt, "2.1. Description of Case Study Location and WDN ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 9.96pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(187.68pt, 133.92pt, "Noja is a seaside village in the north of Spain, in the Cantabria community (Figure 1). ")
  #line-at(166.44pt, 146.64pt, "It is located 43 km east of Santander and 75 west of Bilbao. The total population is 2650 ")
  #line-at(166.44pt, 159.48pt, "habitants [48]. However, mainly during the summer period, bank holidays and Easter, the ")
  #line-at(166.44pt, 172.32pt, "population grows dramatically to up to 80,000 habitants. Indeed, Noja is identified as the ")
  #line-at(166.44pt, 185.16pt, "Spanish town with the highest percentage, 91%, of second residences over the total of res-")
  #line-at(166.44pt, 198pt, "idences in the village [49]. ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 9pt, weight: "bold", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(166.44pt, 470.88pt, "Figure 1. ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 9pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(204.36pt, 470.88pt, "Study area location. ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 9.96pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(187.68pt, 495.24pt, "The population fluctuation between the summer period/bank holidays and the rest ")
  #line-at(166.44pt, 508.08pt, "of the year generates big differences in the total amount of water supplied. Figure 2 depicts ")
  #line-at(166.44pt, 520.92pt, "the total daily flow (TDF) delivered into the network from February 2021 to April 2022. ")
  #line-at(166.44pt, 533.76pt, "During the months of July and August, the TDF reaches its maximum value, an average ")
  #line-at(166.44pt, 546.6pt, "of 5080 m")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 6pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(209.4pt, 544.08pt, "3")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 9.96pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(212.4pt, 546.6pt, "/day with a maximum of 6110 m")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 6pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(356.52pt, 544.08pt, "3")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 9.96pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(359.52pt, 546.6pt, "/day during the Spanish long weekend in the ")
  #line-at(166.44pt, 559.44pt, "middle of August 2021. On the other hand, the minimum TDF values occur during the ")
  #line-at(166.44pt, 572.16pt, "winter months of January/February, with an average of 1262 m")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 6pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(451.08pt, 569.64pt, "3")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 9.96pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(454.08pt, 572.16pt, "/day. During the Easter ")
  #line-at(166.44pt, 585pt, "period, the TDF also increases as a result of more people traveling to the area (week of ")
  #line-at(166.44pt, 597.84pt, "April 2022). In Figure 2, the effect of Easter is evident in 2022 but less so in 2021. This is ")
  #line-at(166.44pt, 610.68pt, "because, in 2022, the COVID pandemic restrictions had already been lifted. ")
]

